The model uses an Earth-centred inertial frame with units of km, s and kg. Gravity is the point-mass term with mu = 398600.4418 km^3/s^2 plus the standard J2 zonal term with J2 = 1.08262668e-3 and R_E = 6378.137 km, z being the Earth'"'"'s spin axis. The only other force is the engine, which produces throttle × 5.0 N along the commanded inertial unit vector (acceleration throttle × 5.0 / m in m/s^2, so divide by 1000 for km/s^2). The specific impulse is 1800 s with g0 = 9.80665 m/s^2, so the mass decreases at throttle × 5.0 / (1800 × 9.80665) kg/s. The Sun direction is fixed along +X. The spacecraft is in eclipse whenever x < 0 and y^2 + z^2 < R_E^2. During eclipse the engine produces no thrust and consumes no propellant, whatever the command says.

At t = 0 the spacecraft is at the perigee of an orbit with perigee altitude 250 km, apogee altitude 35786 km, inclination 28.5 deg, RAAN 0 and argument of perigee 0. Its position is therefore r = (6628.137, 0, 0) km and its velocity is v = (0, v_p cos 28.5 deg, v_p sin 28.5 deg), with v_p given by the vis-viva equation. The final time is fixed at TF = 1555200 s (18 days). At TF the osculating Keplerian elements computed from the Cartesian state must satisfy |a - 42164 km| <= 10 km, e <= 5e-4 and i <= 0.05 deg, and the mass must be at least 1310.0 kg. The distance from the Earth'"'"'s centre must stay at or above R_E + 200 km over the whole interval [0, TF].

/app/control.csv is a comma-separated ASCII file whose first line is exactly t,ux,uy,uz,throttle. Each following row holds five decimal numbers: a time in seconds, an inertial unit vector (norm within 1e-6 of 1) and a throttle in [0, 1]. The first time is 0, each time is at least 1 s after the previous one, the last time is below TF, and the file has at most 200000 rows. Each row is held constant from its own time until the next row'"'"'s time, and the last row holds until TF.

The verifier integrates the file with fixed-step RK4, locating eclipse entries and exits by bisection, once with a 5 s step and once with a 2.5 s step. The two runs must agree to within 1e-3 kg in final mass, 0.1 km in a and 1e-6 in e. All the requirements above are evaluated on the 2.5 s run.

You have 28800 seconds to complete this task. Do not cheat by using online solutions or hints specific to this task.
